+We have conducted an experiment where seed counts are equalized in Section~IV. \tool{} and \sedar{} transfer the same source test cases, and both use the same number of initial seeds (100, 200, and 300) for \griffin{}. Under the same seed count, \tool{} still achieves higher coverage than \sedar{}. Details can be found in \commentref{2.1}.
 
